<title>USA: National Australia Bank files $3 bln shelf.</title>
<headline>National Australia Bank files $3 bln shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Australia Bank Ltd filed Tuesday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission a shelf registration to sell up to $3 billion in debt securities.</p>
<p>Net proceeds will be used for general banking purposes, the filing said.</p>
<p>National Australia, based in Victoria, is Australia's largest bank in terms of assets with total assets of A$173.7 billion as of September 30, 1996.</p>
</text>
